(1148025, 141876, 25468, '<td valign="top">I would have done just the face... the words ruined it for me.</td>', 'I would have done just the face... the words ruined it for me.', '2005-02-02 23:24:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148027, 140587, 25468, '<td valign="top">I''m from Denver so naturally I love the orange and blue. Big fan, great job.</td>', 'I''m from Denver so naturally I love the orange and blue. Big fan, great job.', '2005-02-02 23:25:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148031, 141498, 25468, '<td valign="top">Creepy. And I love creepy! great job.</td>', 'Creepy. And I love creepy! great job.', '2005-02-02 23:26:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148033, 141663, 25468, '<td valign="top">I enjoyed this photo except for the cropping, mostly on the bottom. I think you should have left some negative space to make this better.</td>', 'I enjoyed this photo except for the cropping, mostly on the bottom. I think you should have left some negative space to make this better.', '2005-02-02 23:27:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148035, 141678, 25468, '<td valign="top">I assume you used one of those filters that does this with light reflection. Great application if so. If not, great job.</td>', 'I assume you used one of those filters that does this with light reflection. Great application if so. If not, great job.', '2005-02-02 23:28:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148039, 141687, 25468, '<td valign="top">Awesome. My fav.</td>', 'Awesome. My fav.', '2005-02-02 23:29:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148041, 141892, 25468, '<td valign="top">Don''t know how you managed this one but I love it.</td>', 'Don''t know how you managed this one but I love it.', '2005-02-02 23:31:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148047, 141798, 25468, '<td valign="top">I like and dislike this photo. It almost seems like it''s unfinished. You have a great sky, great forground... Then you have a house that is pretty but blah. You should have done something with it.</td>', 'I like and dislike this photo. It almost seems like it''s unfinished. You have a great sky, great forground... Then you have a house that is pretty but blah. You should have done something with it.', '2005-02-02 23:33:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148049, 141664, 25468, '<td valign="top">I have a feeling you''ll be getting a few DQ requests, but alas not from me. I''ll give you the benefit of the doubt on this one.. Assuming it''s legal, OUTSTANDING.</td>', 'I have a feeling you''ll be getting a few DQ requests, but alas not from me. I''ll give you the benefit of the doubt on this one.. Assuming it''s legal, OUTSTANDING.', '2005-02-02 23:35:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148053, 141518, 25468, '<td valign="top">Awesome, another one of my favs from this challenge.</td>', 'Awesome, another one of my favs from this challenge.', '2005-02-02 23:39:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148058, 141487, 25754, '<td valign="top">Woo Robosapien... we have one too!! lol<br/>well done =)</td>', 'Woo Robosapien... we have one too!! lolwell done =)', '2005-02-02 23:43:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148235, 141699, 8635, '<td valign="top">Great shot, but the border is distracting.</td>', 'Great shot, but the border is distracting.', '2005-02-03 02:27:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148433, 141305, 6999, '<td valign="top">Strong sense of composition, just that little touch of mystery form those two whatever-they-are''s. The natural light is good.</td>', 'Strong sense of composition, just that little touch of mystery form those two whatever-they-are''s. The natural light is good.', '2005-02-03 06:49:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148440, 141758, 6999, '<td valign="top">This is a great fight shot, even without the beam of light. Now do tell - you have surely added that in, haven''t you? The trouble is, no-one even in their wildest moments in the lighting indistry would use a light of such narrow beam to light boxing - and from what i can see here it looks like a PAR lamp anyway, which simply cannot produce a beam that narrow (it must be six inches across where it ''hits'' the boxers face). Also, thing that should be behind it have become brighter in that line, which should not happen (the red roof beam). If you wanted to be more accurate, then the beam should spread considerably as it approaches the ring, cerrtainly seen from this angle. Aside from which, as i said, it was a good enough shot anyway - especially with the sweat flying like that, the sense of controlled power from the fighter on the left, the wonderful look of the referee (and his hands in his pockets).</td>', 'This is a great fight shot, even without the beam of light. Now do tell - you have surely added that in, haven''t you? The trouble is, no-one even in their wildest moments in the lighting indistry would use a light of such narrow beam to light boxing - and from what i can see here it looks like a PAR lamp anyway, which simply cannot produce a beam that narrow (it must be six inches across where it ''hits'' the boxers face). Also, thing that should be behind it have become brighter in that line, which should not happen (the red roof beam). If you wanted to be more accurate, then the beam should spread considerably as it approaches the ring, cerrtainly seen from this angle. Aside from which, as i said, it was a good enough shot anyway - especially with the sweat flying like that, the sense of controlled power from the fighter on the left, the wonderful look of the referee (and his hands in his pockets).', '2005-02-03 07:00:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148443, 141670, 6999, '<td valign="top">I''m a sucker for this kind of stuff - I even have a similar thing entered myself :-) I''m not wholly certain of your treatment of this though. The sense of soft focus seems to work against the feel of the scene, to mask the chaos of pipe-work and surfaces. That could equally be the point, of course.</td>', 'I''m a sucker for this kind of stuff - I even have a similar thing entered myself :-) I''m not wholly certain of your treatment of this though. The sense of soft focus seems to work against the feel of the scene, to mask the chaos of pipe-work and surfaces. That could equally be the point, of course.', '2005-02-03 07:04:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148489, 140881, 6999, '<td valign="top">Kind of like this. I can see your choice in cincludding the shadow, but I think you''ve pushed the structure of the lights and their pole too far out of frame in order to include it, and cropped some of the other fittings on the pole - not suggesting that you include every light on the stand, but I think moving the pole into a stronger plane in the image would make it feel less releated - and the colour, the rust, the texture there, set against the moving train, would be rather fine, i think.</td>', 'Kind of like this. I can see your choice in cincludding the shadow, but I think you''ve pushed the structure of the lights and their pole too far out of frame in order to include it, and cropped some of the other fittings on the pole - not suggesting that you include every light on the stand, but I think moving the pole into a stronger plane in the image would make it feel less releated - and the colour, the rust, the texture there, set against the moving train, would be rather fine, i think.', '2005-02-03 07:59:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148505, 141201, 6999, '<td valign="top">One of those shots that seems to have more impact as a thumbnail than as a full image - I think there are graduations in the tone across the frame that aren''t so apparent at full size. Strong composition, obviously, but just lacks any other major point of interest for me.</td>', 'One of those shots that seems to have more impact as a thumbnail than as a full image - I think there are graduations in the tone across the frame that aren''t so apparent at full size. Strong composition, obviously, but just lacks any other major point of interest for me.', '2005-02-03 08:05:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148509, 141353, 28108, '<td valign="top">Absolutely beautiful. The negative space gives the bird freedom. I love the details on its feathers. Rule of thirds makes it perfect. Good luck!</td>', 'Absolutely beautiful. The negative space gives the bird freedom. I love the details on its feathers. Rule of thirds makes it perfect. Good luck!', '2005-02-03 08:06:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148511, 140925, 6999, '<td valign="top">The upsetting of one''s expectations of zones in photography is strongly done here. Muted sense of progression of light, and of texture in the roof (?) lend just enough contrast to the absolute lines. The almost pointless seeming light adds that moment that is all that is needed to tip it into the real. Lovely work.</td>', 'The upsetting of one''s expectations of zones in photography is strongly done here. Muted sense of progression of light, and of texture in the roof (?) lend just enough contrast to the absolute lines. The almost pointless seeming light adds that moment that is all that is needed to tip it into the real. Lovely work.', '2005-02-03 08:08:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148515, 141899, 6999, '<td valign="top">Splendidly daft, both image and title. Just wonderfully bizarre - frmo the unbelievable frame, the butterfly ... but the title just tops it all. Made me laugh.</td>', 'Splendidly daft, both image and title. Just wonderfully bizarre - frmo the unbelievable frame, the butterfly ... but the title just tops it all. Made me laugh.', '2005-02-03 08:11:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148520, 141755, 6999, '<td valign="top">Enormously subtle, this - and a strong sense of the real. The gentleness of the tonality, and yet the evident care in exposure and processing, makes me wonder if it isn''t one from Mr Ward. Excellent compositional balance, and very non-dpc: most I suspect, will struggle tofind a subject, think it lacks sharpness, think the tonal range is too narrow. There''s a sense of the Monet Lily-pond in some of the colours in the water.</td>', 'Enormously subtle, this - and a strong sense of the real. The gentleness of the tonality, and yet the evident care in exposure and processing, makes me wonder if it isn''t one from Mr Ward. Excellent compositional balance, and very non-dpc: most I suspect, will struggle tofind a subject, think it lacks sharpness, think the tonal range is too narrow. There''s a sense of the Monet Lily-pond in some of the colours in the water.', '2005-02-03 08:15:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148525, 141817, 6999, '<td valign="top">Excellent metallic tones here, very strong composition. Reminds me somewhat of the work of Catherine Jamieson, but she hasn''t submitted in nearly a year, so i''d be surprised. Strong photograph.</td>', 'Excellent metallic tones here, very strong composition. Reminds me somewhat of the work of Catherine Jamieson, but she hasn''t submitted in nearly a year, so i''d be surprised. Strong photograph.', '2005-02-03 08:16:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148530, 141607, 6999, '<td valign="top">Nice composition, great sense of light in two ways. Seems just to have lost some detail in the brighter areas - either processing or just a small sensor camera, I would think - doesn''t quite have that ''ping!'' of sharpness that is liked here. It does, however, have mood: in spades.</td>', 'Nice composition, great sense of light in two ways. Seems just to have lost some detail in the brighter areas - either processing or just a small sensor camera, I would think - doesn''t quite have that ''ping!'' of sharpness that is liked here. It does, however, have mood: in spades.', '2005-02-03 08:22:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148533, 140537, 6999, '<td valign="top">To be picky, I would say silhouetted, rather than back-lit; there''s a difference. It''s a wonderful capture though, enhanced by the suspicion that the coffee guy has turned to look at you as you shot. Slightly mad, and outside of the silhouetting, the rest of the frame is given its grace entirely by light. Top stuff.</td>', 'To be picky, I would say silhouetted, rather than back-lit; there''s a difference. It''s a wonderful capture though, enhanced by the suspicion that the coffee guy has turned to look at you as you shot. Slightly mad, and outside of the silhouetting, the rest of the frame is given its grace entirely by light. Top stuff.', '2005-02-03 08:25:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148537, 141465, 6999, '<td valign="top">One of the troubles wih dpc is that there have been so many set-up shots that one can only take this for one. I''d love it to be a genuine war photographer''s shot, but can''t believe it at all. Wonderfully executed, as it were.</td>', 'One of the troubles wih dpc is that there have been so many set-up shots that one can only take this for one. I''d love it to be a genuine war photographer''s shot, but can''t believe it at all. Wonderfully executed, as it were.', '2005-02-03 08:27:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148540, 141513, 6999, '<td valign="top">I now feel I''d know my way around Narbonne station if I were ever to go there. As strong and distinctive as ever.</td>', 'I now feel I''d know my way around Narbonne station if I were ever to go there. As strong and distinctive as ever.', '2005-02-03 08:29:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148543, 141895, 6999, '<td valign="top">I''ll be surprised if this doesn''t win, certainly of what i''ve seen so far. Very good work, although personally I struggle to see much more than sheer technical excellence in it. It doesn''t <i>move</i> me.</td>', 'I''ll be surprised if this doesn''t win, certainly of what i''ve seen so far. Very good work, although personally I struggle to see much more than sheer technical excellence in it. It doesn''t move me.', '2005-02-03 08:31:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148544, 141794, 6999, '<td valign="top">I suspect strong burning in of corners, except that there''s just enough reality to shade in those areas for me to doubt that. Whatver - it absolutely makes the shot.</td>', 'I suspect strong burning in of corners, except that there''s just enough reality to shade in those areas for me to doubt that. Whatver - it absolutely makes the shot.', '2005-02-03 08:34:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148569, 141593, 5792, '<td valign="top">Nice try, good image. Looks like you did something that I do, process the sky separate from the rest of the image as a way to bring out detail. That part worked but, like me, you need to work on the transition boundary. Something I do is re-select the sky then clone out the boundary transition, like is most apparent on the right side of the image along the horizon line. Sometimes I might need to expand or contract the selection by a pixel or two to setup for cloning. If the sky is in a separate layer then you will have to flatten the affected layers first.</td>', 'Nice try, good image. Looks like you did something that I do, process the sky separate from the rest of the image as a way to bring out detail. That part worked but, like me, you need to work on the transition boundary. Something I do is re-select the sky then clone out the boundary transition, like is most apparent on the right side of the image along the horizon line. Sometimes I might need to expand or contract the selection by a pixel or two to setup for cloning. If the sky is in a separate layer then you will have to flatten the affected layers first.', '2005-02-03 09:07:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148587, 140807, 5792, '<td valign="top">Overall a really nice image. B&amp;W is a good choice for this picture. The bright area on the upper right side along the right border in the background is a slight distraction to the beautifully setup rose. I might have cloned that out to black.</td>', 'Overall a really nice image. B&W is a good choice for this picture. The bright area on the upper right side along the right border in the background is a slight distraction to the beautifully setup rose. I might have cloned that out to black.', '2005-02-03 09:26:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148592, 141881, 5792, '<td valign="top">Reversing horizontal and vertical works well in this image.</td>', 'Reversing horizontal and vertical works well in this image.', '2005-02-03 09:31:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148596, 141175, 5792, '<td valign="top">Funny title, beautiful shot, great advertisement. :)</td>', 'Funny title, beautiful shot, great advertisement. :)', '2005-02-03 09:33:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148603, 139653, 5792, '<td valign="top">Very clever shot.</td>', 'Very clever shot.', '2005-02-03 09:37:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148616, 141783, 20941, '<td valign="top">How perfect for this challenge and so beautifully captured!</td>', 'How perfect for this challenge and so beautifully captured!', '2005-02-03 09:49:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148620, 141649, 20941, '<td valign="top">simple, neat, I like your choice of composition here, interesting how you have an old fashion type scene with the modern light bulb. Maybe a tiny bit less exposure, but this is a light challenge....anyway, I like it 8</td>', 'simple, neat, I like your choice of composition here, interesting how you have an old fashion type scene with the modern light bulb. Maybe a tiny bit less exposure, but this is a light challenge....anyway, I like it 8', '2005-02-03 09:55:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148622, 141347, 20941, '<td valign="top">very cool idea very well executed</td>', 'very cool idea very well executed', '2005-02-03 09:56:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148623, 141487, 11895, '<td valign="top">a lighter background would have better</td>', 'a lighter background would have better', '2005-02-03 09:56:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148624, 139647, 20941, '<td valign="top">a familiar subject in an excellent use of lighting...oooommmm ooooommmmm...ummm my inner soul tells me 9</td>', 'a familiar subject in an excellent use of lighting...oooommmm ooooommmmm...ummm my inner soul tells me 9', '2005-02-03 10:02:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148627, 141222, 20941, '<td valign="top">cool shot, makes me wonder what I''m looking at through the low light and water on the glass</td>', 'cool shot, makes me wonder what I''m looking at through the low light and water on the glass', '2005-02-03 10:05:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148631, 141417, 20941, '<td valign="top">good candid capture for a light challenge. Gives so much depth to an otherwise ordinary scene. guess thats what its all about. Wonderful photo IMO</td>', 'good candid capture for a light challenge. Gives so much depth to an otherwise ordinary scene. guess thats what its all about. Wonderful photo IMO', '2005-02-03 10:08:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148633, 140561, 20941, '<td valign="top">very nice use of light to enhance your well composed subject</td>', 'very nice use of light to enhance your well composed subject', '2005-02-03 10:09:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148641, 141759, 2490, '<td valign="top">Almost too high key for my tastes, but impressive nonetheless.</td>', 'Almost too high key for my tastes, but impressive nonetheless.', '2005-02-03 10:16:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148645, 141212, 2490, '<td valign="top">I like it but something about the snow is colored wrong.  Seems like a bit of a color shift. 7</td>', 'I like it but something about the snow is colored wrong.  Seems like a bit of a color shift. 7', '2005-02-03 10:17:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148646, 141890, 20941, '<td valign="top">cool...not a particularly beautiful image but does demonstrate an interestng use of light and vision. Unique and interesting entry</td>', 'cool...not a particularly beautiful image but does demonstrate an interestng use of light and vision. Unique and interesting entry', '2005-02-03 10:18:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148647, 139856, 2490, '<td valign="top">I love this shot!  Great adaptation of an older idea :) 8</td>', 'I love this shot!  Great adaptation of an older idea :) 8', '2005-02-03 10:20:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148650, 141398, 20941, '<td valign="top">good idea with nice color. Just my opinion, but I might have composed this so that the unattractive metal bottom of the bulb were hidden in the feathers and if you could have found a way to illuminate the bulb for light instead of using an outside source (looks like you used an on camera flash) it might have been even better.</td>', 'good idea with nice color. Just my opinion, but I might have composed this so that the unattractive metal bottom of the bulb were hidden in the feathers and if you could have found a way to illuminate the bulb for light instead of using an outside source (looks like you used an on camera flash) it might have been even better.', '2005-02-03 10:24:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148653, 141899, 20941, '<td valign="top">cool idea I probably would have tried to obscure the view of the cord and metal bottom of the light bulb with something more attractive like another butterfly. But maybe that would interfere with the image you wanted</td>', 'cool idea I probably would have tried to obscure the view of the cord and metal bottom of the light bulb with something more attractive like another butterfly. But maybe that would interfere with the image you wanted', '2005-02-03 10:28:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148655, 141509, 20941, '<td valign="top">beautiful capture of light</td>', 'beautiful capture of light', '2005-02-03 10:29:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148658, 141034, 2490, '<td valign="top">Beautiful picture, I''m just not sure I see that light is the subject.  You still get a 6 :)</td>', 'Beautiful picture, I''m just not sure I see that light is the subject.  You still get a 6 :)', '2005-02-03 10:30:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148659, 141894, 2490, '<td valign="top">Excellent shot.  10.</td>', 'Excellent shot.  10.', '2005-02-03 10:30:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148747, 141513, 20941, '<td valign="top">Good example of how light creates an atmosphere or mood out of an ordinary scene. Coupled with your composition you''ve created an image that is very appealing to me.</td>', 'Good example of how light creates an atmosphere or mood out of an ordinary scene. Coupled with your composition you''ve created an image that is very appealing to me.', '2005-02-03 11:14:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148753, 139612, 20941, '<td valign="top">cool idea well presented hope you hit a moon shot with this :)!</td>', 'cool idea well presented hope you hit a moon shot with this :)!', '2005-02-03 11:18:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148759, 140074, 20941, '<td valign="top">pretty subject well composed. A littile backlight through the pampus grass really makes a beautiful subject but you''ve done well without it.</td>', 'pretty subject well composed. A littile backlight through the pampus grass really makes a beautiful subject but you''ve done well without it.', '2005-02-03 11:22:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1148760, 141391, 20941, '<td valign="top">interesting idea. Looks like it could be a little sharper in focus</td>', 'interesting idea. Looks like it could be a little sharper in focus', '2005-02-03 11:24:41.000000', NULL, 1),
