(1150923, 141875, 8860, '<td valign="top">Nice lead-in lines. The problem here is flash and the lack of a tripod. With a steady camera you could achieve a slower shutter and avoid the use of flash which illuminates the foreground and under-exposes the rest of your background. <br/> <br/>If you focus on the lightest point about 2/3 the way across the bridge, your exposure would work out OK - with all of the shot in focus too.</td>', 'Nice lead-in lines. The problem here is flash and the lack of a tripod. With a steady camera you could achieve a slower shutter and avoid the use of flash which illuminates the foreground and under-exposes the rest of your background.  If you focus on the lightest point about 2/3 the way across the bridge, your exposure would work out OK - with all of the shot in focus too.', '2005-02-04 16:50:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1150926, 141514, 32033, '<td valign="top">Spooky</td>', 'Spooky', '2005-02-04 16:52:51.000000', NULL, 1),
