(1150984, 140315, 5286, '<td valign="top">My eyes go to the stubble and not the feather at all!!<br/>PS: Edited for typo.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-02-07 13:09:03.</i></td>', 'My eyes go to the stubble and not the feather at all!!PS: Edited for typo.', '2005-02-04 17:34:38.000000', '2005-02-07 13:09:03.000000', 1),
(1150996, 141787, 27847, '<td valign="top">Really cool approach to this challenge, I love it. The lighting in this shot is superb in my opinion (wow good lighting in a Light challenge, ha ha). I''m curious, either you have this shot taken with the piece on it''s side standing on a table or something and/or it''s suspended and you cloned out the strings!?!? Hope to find out. Good Job</td>', 'Really cool approach to this challenge, I love it. The lighting in this shot is superb in my opinion (wow good lighting in a Light challenge, ha ha). I''m curious, either you have this shot taken with the piece on it''s side standing on a table or something and/or it''s suspended and you cloned out the strings!?!? Hope to find out. Good Job', '2005-02-04 17:47:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1151000, 141895, 30364, '<td valign="top">This is very impressive and deceptively simple.  It''s a nice scene, which most of us might have dressed up with a strolling or pensive figure in silhouette.  A clever few might have thought to make the figure a photographer, perhaps even with a tripod, to more fully embrace this challenge subject.  But the spread (human) legs were a rare inspiration, and lift this image way above the usual sunrise/sunset shot.  Great work.  9<br/>Second opinion:  My prediction for blue ribbon (could be the kiss of death; my top picks usually finish back in the pack!)</td>', 'This is very impressive and deceptively simple.  It''s a nice scene, which most of us might have dressed up with a strolling or pensive figure in silhouette.  A clever few might have thought to make the figure a photographer, perhaps even with a tripod, to more fully embrace this challenge subject.  But the spread (human) legs were a rare inspiration, and lift this image way above the usual sunrise/sunset shot.  Great work.  9Second opinion:  My prediction for blue ribbon (could be the kiss of death; my top picks usually finish back in the pack!)', '2005-02-04 17:53:43.000000', NULL, 1),
