(1153276, 141188, 1031, '<td valign="top">Good idea, well-done. I like the translucency of the shadows, and the balance between the lit and shadowed parts of the flower.</td>', 'Good idea, well-done. I like the translucency of the shadows, and the balance between the lit and shadowed parts of the flower.', '2005-02-06 12:21:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1153280, 140881, 1031, '<td valign="top">I like you use of a moving background (train?) to contrast with the detail on the lights.</td>', 'I like you use of a moving background (train?) to contrast with the detail on the lights.', '2005-02-06 12:25:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1153282, 141222, 6999, '<td valign="top">Like this very much: the mystery of it, the compositional strength, the strong sense of light. I oftenwonder, with this kind of tonal rnage in an image here (i.e. dpc, or web display generally), whether it isn''t more effective to enhance the low-end curve - from around 0 up to around 20: the variety of different moitor settings and types on which it is going to be viewed have the greatest difference in that kind of range, and it ouwld give you more control over what folks generally see in areas like the left of frame here.</td>', 'Like this very much: the mystery of it, the compositional strength, the strong sense of light. I oftenwonder, with this kind of tonal rnage in an image here (i.e. dpc, or web display generally), whether it isn''t more effective to enhance the low-end curve - from around 0 up to around 20: the variety of different moitor settings and types on which it is going to be viewed have the greatest difference in that kind of range, and it ouwld give you more control over what folks generally see in areas like the left of frame here.', '2005-02-06 12:28:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1153284, 139612, 1031, '<td valign="top">I''d prefer an even narrower angle so that there''s only the specular reflection from one "crater." I really like the idea!</td>', 'I''d prefer an even narrower angle so that there''s only the specular reflection from one "crater." I really like the idea!', '2005-02-06 12:31:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1153285, 141439, 6999, '<td valign="top">Very strong sense of both detail and light, as well as obviously meeting the challenge - a good still life. I wonder if a tiny touch of front fill light would have been useful - or might simply have added unhelpful reflections. It might also have added a yseful sense of plasticity to the main subject, of three-dimensionality. I like your background too - the uneven light there, the texture of the paper(?). Excellent work.</td>', 'Very strong sense of both detail and light, as well as obviously meeting the challenge - a good still life. I wonder if a tiny touch of front fill light would have been useful - or might simply have added unhelpful reflections. It might also have added a yseful sense of plasticity to the main subject, of three-dimensionality. I like your background too - the uneven light there, the texture of the paper(?). Excellent work.', '2005-02-06 12:32:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1153288, 141524, 1031, '<td valign="top">What a great sculpture -- I hope there''s some additional info on this to read later.</td>', 'What a great sculpture -- I hope there''s some additional info on this to read later.', '2005-02-06 12:34:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1153292, 141230, 6999, '<td valign="top">Almost, almost very beautiful. I think you''ve restricted the graduations of light too much for this to be really effective - the highlights are blown, and the transitions into the black areas seem to happen pretty quickly, especially toward the bottom of frame. A little more care in the organisations of the balls, to prevent the seams showing, would have added a touch more neatness too. It could I think, have been a very beautiful shot, but needed a bit more care and attention to the finest level of detail and composition/organisation of elements.</td>', 'Almost, almost very beautiful. I think you''ve restricted the graduations of light too much for this to be really effective - the highlights are blown, and the transitions into the black areas seem to happen pretty quickly, especially toward the bottom of frame. A little more care in the organisations of the balls, to prevent the seams showing, would have added a touch more neatness too. It could I think, have been a very beautiful shot, but needed a bit more care and attention to the finest level of detail and composition/organisation of elements.', '2005-02-06 12:35:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1153296, 140538, 1031, '<td valign="top">Good angle/composition make this a postcard-like shot. I think it might improve just a little if you whiten-up the clouds on the horizon.</td>', 'Good angle/composition make this a postcard-like shot. I think it might improve just a little if you whiten-up the clouds on the horizon.', '2005-02-06 12:38:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1153302, 140825, 1031, '<td valign="top">Hmmm .. can''t let the kids see this one : )</td>', 'Hmmm .. can''t let the kids see this one : )', '2005-02-06 12:39:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1153307, 141789, 6999, '<td valign="top">I''ve been avoiding commenting on this one. There are a number of everso effective elements to it - the general strength of composition, the vignetting (whether edited or natural it is very useful). But there are elements of the composition that don''t really sit very comfortably for me - chiefly your positioning of the bench/tree relative to one another, relative to frame: it leaves me wanting some element toward image left to provide a touch to re-balance things, or perhaps just to balance the composition more to the left, which I realise would mean croping out the end of that branch, but I think that wouldn''t hurt in the same way as that slight upsetting of the balance of things does; these are very minor seeming details, but i think they have an exaggerated impact on the final composition. That hut and background behind the tree I think i would have tried to work/process out of the image too - or, if they''re wanted, to give them more prominence. For dpc certainly, using levels or whatever to black them out would be preferred.</td>', 'I''ve been avoiding commenting on this one. There are a number of everso effective elements to it - the general strength of composition, the vignetting (whether edited or natural it is very useful). But there are elements of the composition that don''t really sit very comfortably for me - chiefly your positioning of the bench/tree relative to one another, relative to frame: it leaves me wanting some element toward image left to provide a touch to re-balance things, or perhaps just to balance the composition more to the left, which I realise would mean croping out the end of that branch, but I think that wouldn''t hurt in the same way as that slight upsetting of the balance of things does; these are very minor seeming details, but i think they have an exaggerated impact on the final composition. That hut and background behind the tree I think i would have tried to work/process out of the image too - or, if they''re wanted, to give them more prominence. For dpc certainly, using levels or whatever to black them out would be preferred.', '2005-02-06 12:43:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1153308, 139433, 1031, '<td valign="top">Oooh ... not many pictures of cloud-to-cloud lightning around -- great capture. I''m sure your local NOAA gallery would be happy to see this.</td>', 'Oooh ... not many pictures of cloud-to-cloud lightning around -- great capture. I''m sure your local NOAA gallery would be happy to see this.', '2005-02-06 12:43:45.000000', NULL, 1),
