(1154378, 141885, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by skiprow:</b></div><hr/><i> nice work, paul!  this really deserved better.  i thought it met the challenge well--<i>without</i> the title.  thanks for another entertaining entry! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks! -- for a change it seems a lot of people felt disposed towards humor : )<br/> <br/>I''d actually had this idea in mind for a long time (months) but, as usual, had to scramble at the last minute to find the scale and get the shot in. (Lack of) focus on the scale I think is due to DOF issues, as I was most concerned with the light/focus on the garlic itself (pretty good, I thought); plus, the scale is pretty ugly in color.<br/> <br/>And I have this other idea for the next time we have a "Light" -related challenge ... of course I forgot to use it this time : )</td>', 'Originally posted by skiprow: nice work, paul!  this really deserved better.  i thought it met the challenge well--without the title.  thanks for another entertaining entry!  Thanks! -- for a change it seems a lot of people felt disposed towards humor : ) I''d actually had this idea in mind for a long time (months) but, as usual, had to scramble at the last minute to find the scale and get the shot in. (Lack of) focus on the scale I think is due to DOF issues, as I was most concerned with the light/focus on the garlic itself (pretty good, I thought); plus, the scale is pretty ugly in color. And I have this other idea for the next time we have a "Light" -related challenge ... of course I forgot to use it this time : )', '2005-02-07 03:13:11.000000', NULL, 0),
