(1154408, 141514, 23458, '<td valign="top">This is stunning - this will no doubt serve as an inspiration to owners of cannon''s trusty point and shoot everywhere!</td>', 'This is stunning - this will no doubt serve as an inspiration to owners of cannon''s trusty point and shoot everywhere!', '2005-02-07 03:53:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154411, 141895, 9668, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your votes and wonderful comments, I was not expecting to have this photo do so highly. This is simply the a view of the glory of creation.<br/> <br/>Ansel Adams once said <i>Sometimes I do get to places just when God''s ready to have somebody click the shutter.</i> I believe that I''m here to capture God''s glory and share it with others. So I hope you enjoy =)</td>', 'Thank you all for your votes and wonderful comments, I was not expecting to have this photo do so highly. This is simply the a view of the glory of creation. Ansel Adams once said Sometimes I do get to places just when God''s ready to have somebody click the shutter. I believe that I''m here to capture God''s glory and share it with others. So I hope you enjoy =)', '2005-02-07 03:56:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154412, 141895, 19959, '<td valign="top">Congrats. This is excellent...</td>', 'Congrats. This is excellent...', '2005-02-07 03:59:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154413, 141518, 23458, '<td valign="top">Predictable perhaps, but continually stunning nonetheless - I like the way you have employed the light here. Congrats on yet another 6.5+ image!</td>', 'Predictable perhaps, but continually stunning nonetheless - I like the way you have employed the light here. Congrats on yet another 6.5+ image!', '2005-02-07 03:59:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154414, 141895, 9668, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by goodman:</b></div><hr/><i> now i wanna know how you could run with camera and tripod?<br/>are you sure you weren''t walking? ;)<br/>brilliant shot of course! </i></td></tr></table>Altough I have run with camera and tripod before (my <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=108843" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Solitude</a> shot was taken on a run back from being dropped off at Haystack), I didn''t have a tripod this time, just my f717 in the camera bag clutched in an arm (alternated from time to time), and a slow-moderate pace. It does turn into a walk when I am shooting though =). I am training for Track season, but my passion for photography and love of running conflict. So this was is my temporary solution (in the future, I''d like to get a small camera that I could run more easily with though).</td>', 'Originally posted by goodman: now i wanna know how you could run with camera and tripod?are you sure you weren''t walking? ;)brilliant shot of course! Altough I have run with camera and tripod before (my Solitude shot was taken on a run back from being dropped off at Haystack), I didn''t have a tripod this time, just my f717 in the camera bag clutched in an arm (alternated from time to time), and a slow-moderate pace. It does turn into a walk when I am shooting though =). I am training for Track season, but my passion for photography and love of running conflict. So this was is my temporary solution (in the future, I''d like to get a small camera that I could run more easily with though).', '2005-02-07 04:01:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154416, 139438, 23458, '<td valign="top">Good job mate - congrats on a terrific score.</td>', 'Good job mate - congrats on a terrific score.', '2005-02-07 04:05:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154418, 141895, 23458, '<td valign="top">Once again this is gorgeous. Though at this point I''ll have to admit I can''t wait for the time when we get to see you put your excellent skills to work on another landscape :P. I guess that''s the curse of still being in school eh :). Good luck with your track season, and congrats on another beautiful image...not to mention the blue ribbon that goes with it.</td>', 'Once again this is gorgeous. Though at this point I''ll have to admit I can''t wait for the time when we get to see you put your excellent skills to work on another landscape :P. I guess that''s the curse of still being in school eh :). Good luck with your track season, and congrats on another beautiful image...not to mention the blue ribbon that goes with it.', '2005-02-07 04:08:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154433, 141895, 22459, '<td valign="top">fantastic image that was a well deserved winner.</td>', 'fantastic image that was a well deserved winner.', '2005-02-07 04:36:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154434, 141755, 30364, '<td valign="top">Most disappointing finish I''ve seen by a genuinely high-quality photograph.  However, there are three reasons for optimism.  First, a few people did recognise its quality.  Second, one of them was Ed Clarke (e301), who is almost certainly the best judge and the most insightful commentator on DPC.  Third, you know how good it is anyway.  Oh, and there''s a fourth ... you can go out tomorrow and produce another image just as good as this one.  <br/>Edit ... Just found a fifth reason; e301 suspected you could be Robt. Ward &amp; if anyone knows about light, it is he.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-02-07 06:07:05.</i></td>', 'Most disappointing finish I''ve seen by a genuinely high-quality photograph.  However, there are three reasons for optimism.  First, a few people did recognise its quality.  Second, one of them was Ed Clarke (e301), who is almost certainly the best judge and the most insightful commentator on DPC.  Third, you know how good it is anyway.  Oh, and there''s a fourth ... you can go out tomorrow and produce another image just as good as this one.  Edit ... Just found a fifth reason; e301 suspected you could be Robt. Ward & if anyone knows about light, it is he.', '2005-02-07 04:37:00.000000', '2005-02-07 06:07:05.000000', 0),
(1154437, 140925, 29462, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your comments and votes<br/> <br/>Pete</td>', 'Thanks for your comments and votes Pete', '2005-02-07 04:47:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154441, 140523, 27482, '<td valign="top">What the hell???  Why didn´t this place higher?  Rediculous!  I didn´t vote in this challenge and this is the first time I have seen it, I would have given it a 10 easily.  I just think this is an awesome show of control of light.</td>', 'What the hell???  Why didn´t this place higher?  Rediculous!  I didn´t vote in this challenge and this is the first time I have seen it, I would have given it a 10 easily.  I just think this is an awesome show of control of light.', '2005-02-07 04:56:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154482, 141783, 8522, '<td valign="top">Superb shot, congrats. You''re an inspiration as to what can be done with Yorkshire countryside!</td>', 'Superb shot, congrats. You''re an inspiration as to what can be done with Yorkshire countryside!', '2005-02-07 05:48:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154494, 141347, 23456, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by RulerZigzag:</b></div><hr/><i> how long did this take?? very nice photo...what did you place the leaf on??? an 8 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well it didn''t take long to do once set up, literally a few seconds and once the mag glass was at the right height it burnt straight away. White paper was placed underneath the leaf in full sun.<br/>Not much I could do about the shadow - it was the only true position I could have the glass in which the leaf would burn.</td>', 'Originally posted by RulerZigzag: how long did this take?? very nice photo...what did you place the leaf on??? an 8   Well it didn''t take long to do once set up, literally a few seconds and once the mag glass was at the right height it burnt straight away. White paper was placed underneath the leaf in full sun.Not much I could do about the shadow - it was the only true position I could have the glass in which the leaf would burn.', '2005-02-07 06:01:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154542, 141843, 23458, '<td valign="top">Sheesh - you just keep coming up with the goods :) - really love this - a nice change from the archtypical sunset shot.</td>', 'Sheesh - you just keep coming up with the goods :) - really love this - a nice change from the archtypical sunset shot.', '2005-02-07 06:46:06.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(1154546, 141535, 23458, '<td valign="top">Stunning. Very stark, in a wonderful way. This is clearly my favourite of your shots here. I quite like the centralised composition - it''s almost as if the ice is cascading down the image, and the background has taken on an almost otherworldly feel.</td>', 'Stunning. Very stark, in a wonderful way. This is clearly my favourite of your shots here. I quite like the centralised composition - it''s almost as if the ice is cascading down the image, and the background has taken on an almost otherworldly feel.', '2005-02-07 06:52:53.000000', NULL, 0),
