(1154754, 141895, 714, '<td valign="top">Very pretty!  Congrats!</td>', 'Very pretty!  Congrats!', '2005-02-07 10:15:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154764, 141895, 32754, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! I knew this would be a winner.</td>', 'Congratulations! I knew this would be a winner.', '2005-02-07 10:25:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154775, 141122, 20679, '<td valign="top">Wow! I am SO excited to have won a ribbon with this shot. I finally made the plunge to become a member just before this challenge was announced and this was my first member entry. I am thrilled to have broken 7 and would have been happy with a top 10 finish (one of my 2005 goals) but a red ribbon....WOW! <br/> <br/>Thanks to everyone for their comments. This challenge had some incredible shots in it and I am honored to be in such fine company :)</td>', 'Wow! I am SO excited to have won a ribbon with this shot. I finally made the plunge to become a member just before this challenge was announced and this was my first member entry. I am thrilled to have broken 7 and would have been happy with a top 10 finish (one of my 2005 goals) but a red ribbon....WOW!  Thanks to everyone for their comments. This challenge had some incredible shots in it and I am honored to be in such fine company :)', '2005-02-07 10:32:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154785, 141895, 8125, '<td valign="top">Great choice for the challenge... wow ... this is fantastic!  Going in my favorites for sure.  Congrats on the blue!</td>', 'Great choice for the challenge... wow ... this is fantastic!  Going in my favorites for sure.  Congrats on the blue!', '2005-02-07 10:39:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154787, 141260, 3419, '<td valign="top">You know what? I rather like this one. It''s really simple, but abstract. I wouldn''t have guessed what it is. The closest I came to guessing what it is, is a backlit slide or other type of transparency object. I can definitely see this as a framed print in a modern-decor environment (you know, the type of decor that uses stainless steel in furniture and fixtures, etc). Adding this to my favourites.</td>', 'You know what? I rather like this one. It''s really simple, but abstract. I wouldn''t have guessed what it is. The closest I came to guessing what it is, is a backlit slide or other type of transparency object. I can definitely see this as a framed print in a modern-decor environment (you know, the type of decor that uses stainless steel in furniture and fixtures, etc). Adding this to my favourites.', '2005-02-07 10:43:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154816, 141895, 20679, '<td valign="top">A spectacular shot, Thomas. I feel honored to have come in 2nd to this. Well done and congratulations :)</td>', 'A spectacular shot, Thomas. I feel honored to have come in 2nd to this. Well done and congratulations :)', '2005-02-07 11:09:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154830, 141564, 11843, '<td valign="top">Yeah, that is really nice shot. Great work!</td>', 'Yeah, that is really nice shot. Great work!', '2005-02-07 11:21:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154852, 140567, 28023, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone for their comments. Just got this camera and have never entered anything before so I suppose this was a way to get the feet wet. Doesn''t help that I don''t have access to Photoshop yet which is why I had trouble with sizing. Anyway, hopefully I can tweak the rudimentary stuff and submit more meaningful shots in the future. <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Britannica:</b></div><hr/><i> The points that I am sure you have heard already in the comments; image size is not using the allowed size of 640 pixels on a side and has a bit of a clockwise tilt.  The motion blur is so obvious I will assume it was intentional, and it certainly brings the focus of the image away from the building (as a building) and places it squarely on the lights.  A great way to meet the challenge topic head on.  However, abstracting the building in this way leaves you with composition only to produce an effect -- and it is a bit heavy on the right hand side.  The large bright area in the lower right out weights the rest of the image -- I believe placing more negative space on the right and less on the left would have produced a better composed image. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Thanks to everyone for their comments. Just got this camera and have never entered anything before so I suppose this was a way to get the feet wet. Doesn''t help that I don''t have access to Photoshop yet which is why I had trouble with sizing. Anyway, hopefully I can tweak the rudimentary stuff and submit more meaningful shots in the future.  Originally posted by Britannica: The points that I am sure you have heard already in the comments; image size is not using the allowed size of 640 pixels on a side and has a bit of a clockwise tilt.  The motion blur is so obvious I will assume it was intentional, and it certainly brings the focus of the image away from the building (as a building) and places it squarely on the lights.  A great way to meet the challenge topic head on.  However, abstracting the building in this way leaves you with composition only to produce an effect -- and it is a bit heavy on the right hand side.  The large bright area in the lower right out weights the rest of the image -- I believe placing more negative space on the right and less on the left would have produced a better composed image. ', '2005-02-07 11:41:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154927, 141709, 32754, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all of you for taking time to critique and your helpful comments. I am a relative novice to digital photography; I keep trying new techniques; it is such fun.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-02-07 12:27:32.</i></td>', 'Thanks to all of you for taking time to critique and your helpful comments. I am a relative novice to digital photography; I keep trying new techniques; it is such fun.', '2005-02-07 12:27:10.000000', '2005-02-07 12:27:32.000000', 0),
