(1155778, 141044, 6999, '<td valign="top">I really can''t believe that this only just scraped a 6. Sure the angle has probably cost a few points, but really. My suspicion is that simply because it <i>looks</i> so photoshopped (and I mean very skillfully photoshopped) ... but that vote curve is pretty evenly centred around the 6 point. I think you have perhaps suffered from the fact that this was an advanced editing challenge.<br/> <br/>+fav</td>', 'I really can''t believe that this only just scraped a 6. Sure the angle has probably cost a few points, but really. My suspicion is that simply because it looks so photoshopped (and I mean very skillfully photoshopped) ... but that vote curve is pretty evenly centred around the 6 point. I think you have perhaps suffered from the fact that this was an advanced editing challenge. +fav', '2005-02-07 19:28:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1155872, 141783, 9581, '<td valign="top">Man that is awesome, Fugi has got a great line of cameras I am really impressed... Instead of saving up for my dream camera the canon rebel I might just have to go a couple of upgrades higher and stick with fugi...This is really impressive! Congrats on third!</td>', 'Man that is awesome, Fugi has got a great line of cameras I am really impressed... Instead of saving up for my dream camera the canon rebel I might just have to go a couple of upgrades higher and stick with fugi...This is really impressive! Congrats on third!', '2005-02-07 20:12:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1155914, 140315, 31408, '<td valign="top">I feel for your voting woes Nick. The "Light" challenge description intentionally included the language<br/> <br/> "Any definition of the word is acceptable for this challenge" <br/> <br/>and that should be the judging standard for that aspect of the score. For someone to broadly adjust their voting score because they personally would prefer a more narrow definition smacks of egotism and does little for the photographers participating, unless you include discouragement as a goal. <br/> <br/>The image is in clear focus and well lit. However as othes have said, the facial hair is scraggly and distracting and the overall impact is lessened for me. <br/> <br/>Maybe I''ll also take points off for it being in Black &amp; White...I don''t think they should be in the challenge  ; )<br/></td>', 'I feel for your voting woes Nick. The "Light" challenge description intentionally included the language  "Any definition of the word is acceptable for this challenge"  and that should be the judging standard for that aspect of the score. For someone to broadly adjust their voting score because they personally would prefer a more narrow definition smacks of egotism and does little for the photographers participating, unless you include discouragement as a goal.  The image is in clear focus and well lit. However as othes have said, the facial hair is scraggly and distracting and the overall impact is lessened for me.  Maybe I''ll also take points off for it being in Black & White...I don''t think they should be in the challenge  ; )', '2005-02-07 20:47:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(1156087, 139982, 16882, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bear_music:</b></div><hr/><i> I quite like this. I suspect it will do very poorly, especially because a poorly-calibrated monitor willnot show the separation of branches and sky at the top. But I good score from me, and I admire the urge to post it despite its total deviation from what''s considered a "winning" approach in DPC. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks, your right it looks much better at 11x17</td>', 'Originally posted by bear_music: I quite like this. I suspect it will do very poorly, especially because a poorly-calibrated monitor willnot show the separation of branches and sky at the top. But I good score from me, and I admire the urge to post it despite its total deviation from what''s considered a "winning" approach in DPC.   Thanks, your right it looks much better at 11x17', '2005-02-07 21:48:27.000000', NULL, 0),
