(1157728, 141514, 31282, '<td valign="top">Woooow congratulations on this great 8 finish ,it was really deserved because the pic is stunning.I knew you were good at photography , with this challenge you show it to everybody.I''m sure you will get a ribbon soon , you just have to keep up the good work ;-)</td>', 'Woooow congratulations on this great 8 finish ,it was really deserved because the pic is stunning.I knew you were good at photography , with this challenge you show it to everybody.I''m sure you will get a ribbon soon , you just have to keep up the good work ;-)', '2005-02-08 16:39:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1157846, 141486, 9581, '<td valign="top">This is pretty clever! You have some awesome ideas.. Usually I am not that picky but it sometimes help to try to point things out that will make the shot more effective.. Then next time you are shooting you start to become aware of these things. There is something like a arm chair beside her that  is changing the way the light flows, maybe throw a sheet solid cover over this you can stack something on the other side or use a broom stick to even it up on the other side.. Or just have your model move over to hide it.. was there light behind her? If so then that may be why the affect of this surprise isnt as strong.. I am starting to play with light more and theres so many affects that when you are trying to accomplish an image you really have to take a ton of pics. All the while during the process move the lights to different spots... Even a foil or mirror can change the light.. I love mirror affects.. I still like this though so dont take me the wrong the way :)</td>', 'This is pretty clever! You have some awesome ideas.. Usually I am not that picky but it sometimes help to try to point things out that will make the shot more effective.. Then next time you are shooting you start to become aware of these things. There is something like a arm chair beside her that  is changing the way the light flows, maybe throw a sheet solid cover over this you can stack something on the other side or use a broom stick to even it up on the other side.. Or just have your model move over to hide it.. was there light behind her? If so then that may be why the affect of this surprise isnt as strong.. I am starting to play with light more and theres so many affects that when you are trying to accomplish an image you really have to take a ton of pics. All the while during the process move the lights to different spots... Even a foil or mirror can change the light.. I love mirror affects.. I still like this though so dont take me the wrong the way :)', '2005-02-08 17:37:57.000000', NULL, 0),
